{"name":"Balsam of Peru","hex":"#120d07","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"balsam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet-smelling oil or resin derived from various plants.","A plant or tree yielding such substance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat or anoint with balsam."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balsam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Balsam of Peru","blocks":[{"text":"Balsam of Peru or Peru balsam, also known and marketed by many other names, is a balsam derived from a tree known as Myroxylon balsamum var. pereirae; it is found in Central and South America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Balsamum_peruvianum1.JPG/330px-Balsamum_peruvianum1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balsam_of_Peru","wikidata":"Q120424"},{"title":"Balsam","blocks":[{"text":"Balsam is the resinous exudate which forms on certain kinds of trees and shrubs, particularly species belonging to genera such as Myroxylon, Abies, Copaifera, Styrax, and Populus. They may occur naturally as resinous exudates following injury to bark or wood tissues. Balsam owes its name to the biblical Balm of Gilead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Balsamum_tolutanum1.JPG/330px-Balsamum_tolutanum1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balsam","wikidata":"Q1776037"},{"title":"Peru","blocks":[{"text":"Peru, officially the Republic of Peru, is a country in western South America. It is bordered to the north by Ecuador and Colombia, to the east by Brazil, to the southeast by Bolivia, to the south by Chile, and to the south and west by the Pacific Ocean. Peru is a megadiverse country, with habitats ranging from the arid plains of the Pacific coastal region in the west, to the peaks of the Andes mountains extending from the north to the southeast of the country, to the tropical Amazon basin rainforest in the east with the Amazon River. Peru has a population of over 32 million, and its capital and largest city is Lima. At 1,285,216 km2 (496,225 sq mi), Peru is the 19th largest country in the world, and the third largest in South America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Flag_of_Peru.svg/330px-Flag_of_Peru.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peru","wikidata":"Q419"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Result_of_standard_T.R.U.E_patch_test_showing_allergy_to_Balsam_of_Peru.jpg/500px-Result_of_standard_T.R.U.E_patch_test_showing_allergy_to_Balsam_of_Peru.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Result_of_standard_T.R.U.E_patch_test_showing_allergy_to_Balsam_of_Peru.jpg/1280px-Result_of_standard_T.R.U.E_patch_test_showing_allergy_to_Balsam_of_Peru.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Result_of_standard_T.R.U.E_patch_test_showing_allergy_to_Balsam_of_Peru.jpg/500px-Result_of_standard_T.R.U.E_patch_test_showing_allergy_to_Balsam_of_Peru.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This T.R.U.E. (Thin-Layer Rapid Use Epicutaneous) Patch Test\n[31]\nresult shows strong reaction to balsam of Peru (#10) and mild reaction to the standard fragrance mix (#6)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AResult_of_standard_T.R.U.E_patch_test_showing_allergy_to_Balsam_of_Peru.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Myroxylon_peruiferum.jpg/500px-Myroxylon_peruiferum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2